<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin says to cut unemployment premiums.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin says to cut unemployment premiums.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin on Friday said the federal government would cut the unemployment insurance premiums as quickly as possible.</p>
<p>&quot;We are going to bring them down as quickly as we conceivably can,&quot; Martin told reporters after a parliamentary session.</p>
<p>Martin was asked if the government might cut the unemployment insurance premiums to offset a proposed rise in the Canadian Pension Plan contributions. He said the two issues were separate.</p>
</text>
